  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788484",
      "title": "Managing & Creating Components with the Angular CLI",
      "lectureOrder": 18,
      "videoOrder": 15,
      "sourceHash": "4def18c43b583f8e78e96b25ab559638557cc3a4c7c6fb57660bf52e92397aac",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 3.36,
          "en": "So we built our first custom component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.36,
          "end": 6.03,
          "en": "from scratch, the header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.03,
          "end": 8.31,
          "en": "And that is something you'll do a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.31,
          "end": 9.78,
          "en": "when working with Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.78,
          "end": 12.483,
          "en": "because you'll be working with a lot of Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 15.45,
          "en": "Now, as you can imagine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.45,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "if you build more and more Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 21.24,
          "en": "since most Components consist of multiple files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.24,
          "end": 25.47,
          "en": "the app folder will grow rather quickly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.47,
          "end": 27.93,
          "en": "and managing all those component files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.93,
          "end": 31.02,
          "en": "can become rather cumbersome quickly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.02,
          "end": 34.05,
          "en": "That's why it's common to put component files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.05,
          "end": 38.103,
          "en": "into subfolders inside of that src app folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.97,
          "end": 41.88,
          "en": "For example, here we could create a new subfolder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.88,
          "end": 45.543,
          "en": "called header for the header component files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.38,
          "end": 48.78,
          "en": "and the convention is to use a folder name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.78,
          "end": 51.87,
          "en": "that just describes the feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.87,
          "end": 56.343,
          "en": "the component is being used for, so the header in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.54,
          "end": 60.27,
          "en": "So we could then grab these three files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.27,
          "end": 62.733,
          "en": "and move them into this header folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.44,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "Now with them moved, you should just make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 70.2,
          "en": "that in the app component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.2,
          "end": 73.833,
          "en": "this import path here is updated accordingly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 78.39,
          "en": "Many IDEs and code editors will do that automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 80.73,
          "en": "but you should double check to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.73,
          "end": 83.61,
          "en": "that you are now importing the header component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.61,
          "end": 85.443,
          "en": "from that header folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.18,
          "end": 89.34,
          "en": "And with that, if you save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.34,
          "end": 91.74,
          "en": "the app should still work as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.74,
          "end": 94.503,
          "en": "but now we have a better folder structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.64,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "That's not the only thing you can and should do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 103.65299999999999,
          "en": "to work with Components more efficiently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 107.75999999999999,
          "en": "Instead, you can also use the Angular CLI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.75999999999999,
          "end": 112.17,
          "en": "to get some help with creating and managing Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 115.5,
          "en": "because let's say we wanna add another component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.5,
          "end": 116.78999999999999,
          "en": "to this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.78999999999999,
          "end": 120.24,
          "en": "a component that will output an individual user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.24,
          "end": 124.89,
          "en": "which we can select to view the tasks of that user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.89,
          "end": 128.76,
          "en": "Now we could, of course, manually create a user folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.76,
          "end": 131.7,
          "en": "and then add all those component files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.7,
          "end": 133.41,
          "en": "and that wouldn't be wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.41,
          "end": 136.29,
          "en": "And indeed, I personally often create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.29,
          "end": 137.763,
          "en": "new Components like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.78,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "But you can also use the Angular CLI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 146.76,
          "en": "and run the generate command to generate a new component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.76,
          "end": 148.82999999999998,
          "en": "for example, for this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.82999999999998,
          "end": 150.75,
          "en": "You can also generate other things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.75,
          "end": 152.55,
          "en": "but here we need a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.55,
          "end": 156.423,
          "en": "and you do that by running ng generate component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.53,
          "end": 161.53,
          "en": "or you can actually shorten this to ng g c",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.63,
          "end": 167.22,
          "en": "and then the name and path of your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.22,
          "end": 171.48,
          "en": "So for example, user, if you wanna create a new user folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.48,
          "end": 174.183,
          "en": "with the user component files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.1,
          "end": 178.05,
          "en": "If you then hit Enter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.05,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "the Angular CLI will go ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 185.75,
          "en": "and create some files for you in a newly added user folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.2,
          "end": 189.45,
          "en": "And of course, we can see that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.45,
          "end": 192.15,
          "en": "in our project structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.15,
          "end": 196.71,
          "en": "This user folder was now added by the CLI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.71,
          "end": 201.39,
          "en": "and in there, you find the user.component.html file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.39,
          "end": 203.04,
          "en": "so it's automatically following",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.04,
          "end": 206.55,
          "en": "that naming convention I described before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 206.55,
          "end": 209.16,
          "en": "the user.component.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.16,
          "end": 211.8,
          "en": "and the user.component.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.8,
          "end": 213.273,
          "en": "which is empty at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.5,
          "end": 218.94,
          "en": "You also find a user.component.spec.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.94,
          "end": 221.4,
          "en": "which is used for automated testing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.4,
          "end": 223.32,
          "en": "and we can delete that right now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.32,
          "end": 226.62,
          "en": "since we'll dive into automated tests later in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.62,
          "end": 228.42000000000002,
          "en": "not right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.42000000000002,
          "end": 231.27,
          "en": "But with that, we now got the same three files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.27,
          "end": 233.91,
          "en": "which we previously created manually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.91,
          "end": 237.6,
          "en": "now created automatically by the CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.6,
          "end": 240.21,
          "en": "In the user.component.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.21,
          "end": 242.55,
          "en": "you also see that it automatically set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.55,
          "end": 244.47,
          "en": "a fitting selector for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.47,
          "end": 247.35,
          "en": "following that naming convention I described before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.35,
          "end": 251.31,
          "en": "and set up the links to the external style files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.31,
          "end": 253.38,
          "en": "It also sets standalone to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 253.38,
          "end": 256.11,
          "en": "since that's the recommended default nowadays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.11,
          "end": 258.03,
          "en": "and added this imports array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 258.03,
          "end": 260.61,
          "en": "in case we would wanna use other Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.61,
          "end": 262.53,
          "en": "inside of that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 265.89300000000003,
          "en": "We can delete it if we don't plan on doing that though.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
